.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "SystemEx\&.Utils\&.BitIntSpan\&.BitIntSpan (ref int value, short startPos, short endPos, \fBFlexSpanMode\fP mode)"

.PP
Initializes a new \fBBitIntSpan\fP that exposes a bit-level view over the referenced \fIvalue\fP \&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvalue\fP A reference to the underlying int whose bits will be read and modified directly\&. No copy is made\&. 
.br
\fIstartPos\fP The starting bit position of the view (inclusive)\&. Must be within the valid bit range of the underlying integer\&. 
.br
\fIendPos\fP The ending bit position of the view (exclusive)\&. Must be greater than \fIstartPos\fP  and within the integer's bit width\&. 
.br
\fImode\fP The indexing mode used to interpret bit positions: \fBFlexSpanMode\&.System\fP, \fBFlexSpanMode\&.Reverse\fP, or \fBFlexSpanMode\&.Ring\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBWarning:\fP This constructor creates a span-like structure that operates directly on a referenced integer\&. All bit reads and writes mutate the original value in-place\&. Multiple spans referencing the same integer will observe and affect each other's changes\&. 

.PP
Because \fBBitIntSpan\fP is a \fRref struct\fP, it is restricted to stack-only usage\&. It cannot be boxed, stored on the heap, used in async methods, or captured by closures\&. 

.PP
Incorrect window boundaries or misuse of \fBFlexSpanMode\&.Ring\fP may lead to out-of-range exceptions or infinite iteration\&. This API is intended for advanced developers who fully understand bit-level operations\&. 
.PP
